UPDATE "search_executions" SET "findings_note" = 'PRIOR HELD, AND THE ONE HIT IT PREDICTED IS THE BATCH HEADLINE. Crossref deposits 117 reference entries, 81 carrying DOIs. The full text was NOT needed -- batch 15 deferred this pass on a Taylor & Francis 403, and the deposited reference list makes the same mining tractable without it, which is the reusable lesson. 6 of 117 pass the ramp/slope/gradient/barrier screen. Five are qualitative barrier or policy work, exactly as predicted. The sixth is Vredenburgh, Hedge, Zackowitz and Weiner 2009, Evaluation of wheelchair users perceived sidewalk and ramp slope: effort and accessibility -- carrying NO DOI in the deposit, so it is invisible to any DOI-keyed pass and had to be resolved by title. It is a wheelchair-user PERCEPTION experiment that states a maximum running slope, which is the exact object GAP-002 names as missing. Admitted under M3 exec so the admission sits with the pass that produced the corroborating anchors; recorded here as the discovery. || CORRECTED 2026-09-27: RC5 phase 2-data (DR-2026-09-26 5.2d): mined_ref_id derived -- this row''s own query_text names exactly one REF id that exists in evidence_sources. || RC1/RC5 phase 2-data (DR-2026-09-26): result-payload link(s) derived from this search''s own query_text against the retrieval log, per section 2.1''s rule. (1 artefact(s)) || CORRECTED 2026-09-27: mined_ref_id set to ''REF-00977'' || CORRECTED 2026-09-27: result artefact(s) added: retrieval-log/session_2026-09-18-research-batch-16-backward-mining-t2-anchors/97df3e4bd28d57e0.json', "mined_ref_id" = 'REF-00977' WHERE "exec_id" = 68;
